_module_matches arm 3 ("dropped qualification") compares trailing
components after casefolding BOTH sides, discarding the one signal that
separates java's `System` — an unqualified reference to the class
java.lang.System — from go's `context`, a parameter of type *cli.Context
spelled like the trailing component of github.com/gin-gonic/gin.Context.
sops's context.String("input-type"), a urfave/cli flag read, reached a
net_send row. That is INV-safig's remedy biting back: appending the type
to the import path is what put Context in trailing position.

THE FIX IS CASE AGREEMENT, NOT A CAPITALISATION TEST, and the item's own
first step warned the obvious fix was not obviously right. Arm 2 asks
whether a component IS capitalised — Go's "capitals mean types", in a
predicate that takes no language and serves fifteen catalogues, carrying
no information where module names are capitalised (haskell 100%, swift
97%, objc 95%, elixir 52%). Arm 3 now asks only whether the two sides are
SPELLED THE SAME WAY. Language-neutral: in those same languages both
sides are capitalised, so they agree and every prior match survives.

WHAT IT MUST NOT COST, each pinned by a named test: java.lang.System <-
System keeps matching (INV-januj and INV-hahak both depend on this arm;
breaking it re-loses java's only ipc_recv row), and so do go's filepath
<- path/filepath and grpc <- google.golang.org/grpc, which INV-dijor
names as true positives at risk from fix (a).

MEASURED, BOTH DIRECTIONS. Catalogue-wide: all 1,090 rows with a
capitalised trailing component now refuse a variable-spelled hint, while
3,954 correctly-cased hints still match and ZERO break. End-to-end on the
filed repo, both arms cold in their own XDG_CACHE_HOME with the baseline
asserted by grepping the runtime file: 159 chains -> 157, REMOVED 2,
ADDED 0 — exactly the two calls INV-dijor filed, inputStore
(main.go:2383) and outputStore, both READ BACK AGAINST SOURCE as
urfave/cli flag reads. Control alive in the same run: context.Deadline ->
None, os.Open still resolves, and String still reaches gin.Context from
the hint it is FOR.

This is EVIDENCE, not the declaration ADR-0051 anticipates — case
disagreement is a proxy for "the hint names a variable, not an owner
path", not a per-row declaration. Arm 2's case-VALUE inference is
untouched and is the residual (WI-zozun).

11,212 tests pass, 100% coverage, mypy ratchet clean.

